<title>FRANCE: BNP suspends plan for U.S. issue.</title>
<headline>BNP suspends plan for U.S. issue.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>French bank Banque Nationale de Paris (BNP) said on Thursday it had decided to suspend plans for a subordinated issue on the U.S. market because of a newspaper article in the French press involving the privatisation of French bank CIC.</p>
<p>A bank spokeswoman could give no further details.</p>
<p>Business daily Les Echos reported Thursday morning that BNP seemed better placed than Societe Generale to take over CIC which is part of state-owned insurer GAN.</p>
<p>The newspaper said that France's privatisation committee could make its decision known later on Thursday on the admissibility of the offers from Societe Generale and BNP.</p>
</text>
